{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1144415-the-newly-awakened","id":1144415,"title":"The newly awakened","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-27T08:00:12-07:00","id":1144415,"title":"The newly awakened","content":"When you start a new game after the characters have gone through their awakening how do you handle orders? Do you just have the players pick which orders they want? Do you have pre made mentors that bring them into orders or do you have the local awakened community watch them from afar testing them to see which orders will have them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T09:47:31-07:00","id":1144466,"title":"","content":"Very few Mages Awaken in an area occupied by the Orders without the Orders knowing about it, and a lot of them have been pre-vetted (before they Awaken even) by the Guardians who will pass them along to Orders they might fit in well with.<br /> <br /> The Seers obviously try and stay ahead of the Guardians, or to poach prospects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T05:19:20-07:00","id":1144710,"title":"","content":"I think most orders first try to incorporate them into their ranks, but maybe after some fate/time readings the pentacle mages decide it\u00b4s better for the new mage to get to know another order. <br /> But characters with dream/destiny i might consider to naturally wind up with the most appropiate order.<br /> <br /> seers kill those who they can\u00b4t persuade or intimidate to join.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T19:32:15-07:00","id":1147911,"title":"","content":"The Orders books specify their recrutement and conversion policies and it's interresting to note that despite what we can assume from the corebooks, the freedom and opportunites for a mage to choose his order are far from assured.<br /> <br /> Basically all Orders try to recruit any new mages they find but can try to give them to the other orders if they are not a good fit, the Silver Ladder and the Mysterium are generally weary of mages coming from other orders (especially if they are established members trying to convert and if they are from the Free Council) and will try to redirect them to the more accepting Adamantine Arrow and depending on the local policies or the petitionner could outright refuse to take them in at all.<br /> <br /> Most mages are indeed found by the Guardians with most of them deemed unfit for the Order, so most of them are passed down to the other orders with more acceptance because their sheer numbers would made that foolish and the Guardians generally (at least officialy) don't groom them enough to make them converts if they try to join another order.<br /> A mage found for example by the Arrow is far more likely to have been virtually made a member before they can try to leave. (And the other orders can afford to be pickier than what all those found by the Guardians)<br /> Obviously such things vary from Caucus to Caucus, but it's likely that a lot will have an agreement that any mage found by an Order is *their*, will often stick to mages they find themselves to avoid political conflicts with the other orders or because they are are too afraid of spies.<br /> <br /> (And obviously a mage generally become a member of the Sect finding him and can't leave, and it's true in a lesser measure even in the Pentacle between the Diamond Orders and the Free Council)<br /> <br /> I guess that this can cause problems when someone really don't fit in an Order and the others will not take them in (especially with the Arrow as they far more eager to accept converts and military life is not for everyone) but some become apostates or choose to join the less focused Free Council for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T10:29:39-07:00","id":1148053,"title":"","content":"From an OOC, Gamemaster talking to players perspective, I turn this question around on them. Things like how long they have been Awakened, how they joined their Order, and if they have a dedicated Mentor are all important character points, and the players should be encouraged to come up with the answers for you, though you should be happy to introduce idea's, setting details and NPC concepts as required, of course. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T02:40:18-07:00","id":1148256,"title":"","content":"Katana 1515 made good points.<br /> <br /> Even when your PC\u00b4s were first discovered by a certain order, let there be a little bluebooking time after the awakening. Don\u00b4t forget that most orders use divination or do test to see if a new mage fits into his desired order. So they can come up with the idea how and why their order choose them, or why they joined it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}